  "diagnostics": "An initial artisan route listing ran under unsafe default production settings and was refused by the existing production safety gate; the explicit testing route listing succeeded. Initial npm shell path inference failed; an explicit locked Node/npm wrapper then installed/tested/audited/built successfully. Initial focused review test restored an incorrect legacy account label; the fixture now restores legacy-primary. Early matrices were intentionally stopped before bounded-version and readable-note assertions. Those assertions exposed the actual Filament notification body signature (string, not HtmlString); the application now supplies escaped string HTML, and real UI success plus inert markup is asserted. Intermediate focused checks also used an unsupported assertNotified Closure and a missing import; final tests use the supported title assertion/session payload. The first frozen-source complete regression exposed a real random Bingo draw_date unique collision in ModelFactoryIntegrityTest. That diagnostic is preserved. The final source repairs all three same-pattern synthetic dated factories and adds distinct repeated-seed/exhaustion tests; final matrices and isolated controls use a new source freeze and disposable stores. Earlier partial/stopped/mutated runs are not regression passes.",
  "scope": "Local synthetic application acceptance only. The new route receives locally signed mock Stripe snapshots, not real merchant traffic. No live Stripe request/event, refund/dispute submission, external transfer, production migration, remote CI or worldwide approval occurred. Default/native profiles overlap;154 default skips remain outside this narrow native selection. Three review races prove two genuine wallet-lock waiters, single case/observation or acknowledgement, and stale-refusal new-evidence retention; the fourth is the prior two-four-GET capture race. Simultaneous raw ingress duplicate races, cross-account/global writer/permission fences and OS-kill/power-loss are not certified. The lower-ID publication and rollback/permission boundaries are controlled fixtures/injected faults. History is limited to5000 account/configuration inbox rows and100 case observations, refusing saturation. Only this dedicated signed inbox is consumed; legacy Applied payment webhooks are not imported. Inspection is explicit; receipt arrival does not immediately reopen a header. Acknowledgement describes the inspected SQL snapshot, not unknown/concurrent/later remote events or a global ingress fence, and never resolves money, restricts withdrawals or proves no refund/dispute. Original account/key migration, generic latest-Applied report adjudication and the remaining release/merchant/country work stay explicit in docs/remaining-work-part-56.md. Synthetic factory date allocation is not production scheduling or cross-process reservation authority."
}
